# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH at its experimental equilibrium bond
# length (r_e = 1.5949 Angstrom, NIST CCCBDB), 6-31G basis (downloaded
# from https://www.basissetexchange.org/, lih-6-31g.gbs), evaluating
# GNOF with TWO independent PNOF coupling subspaces (PNOF_SUBSPACES 2):
# subspace 1 couples HOMO with LUMO, subspace 2 (a DISJOINT block of
# orbitals -- see Input.h's own pnof_subspaces()/pnof_coupling() header
# comments) couples HOMO-1 with LUMO+1, PNOF_COUPLING 2 each (plain
# pairing, one occupied pair to one unoccupied pair per subspace).
# LiH's 4 electrons = exactly 2 occupied pairs (Li 1s core + the Li-H
# bonding pair), so BOTH become frontier (active) geminals here -- no
# frozen core -- specifically to exercise Hessian_opt/PnofFock.h's
# generalized Fock/gradient and the e^kappa orbital-rotation finite-
# difference check (main.cpp's buildPnofFunctionalReport, DEBUG TRUE
# below) with MORE THAN ONE active electron pair/geminal-pair coupling,
# unlike h2_X2C_gnof.inp's single-pair case.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
DEBUG TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
